# GateMPC public-repository allowlist
#
# Everything at the repository root is private by default. Only what a reader or reviewer
# needs in order to rerun the study and check its numbers is allowed below: the software,
# the normalized data package with its provenance and checksums, the experiment scripts
# named in the Data Availability Statement, the result files those scripts write, and the
# tests.
#
# Deliberately NOT published: the manuscript and its working files (paper/), the journal
# template (template/), the reference PDFs (references/, publisher copyright), the internal
# planning, requirement and audit notes (requirements/, Model/, Scopus/), the reviewer
# files and closure reports (reviews/, review_reports/), and every local build product
# (build/).

/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- repository metadata
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/LICENSE.*
!/CITATION.cff
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/requirements-lock.txt
!/requirements-gui.txt
!/.github/
!/.github/**

# Images the README shows. Every path named in public text must lead to a public file,
# so the screenshot the README embeds lives here rather than in build/.
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/explorer.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- application and package
!/main.py
!/pyproject.toml
!/requirements.txt
!/src/
!/src/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- reproducibility tests
!/tests/
!/tests/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- data package
# The normalized USGS/Reclamation layers, the provenance file that records every source
# URL, access date, licence and query, the ASCE Test Case 2 reconstruction, and the
# SHA-256 checksums that make the build its own regression test.
# Raw downloads stay out; the download script must be able to rebuild them.
!/DATA/
/DATA/*
# The dedication that covers the package. `/DATA/*` above re-ignores everything
# directly under DATA/, so this has to be named explicitly -- README.md links to it.
!/DATA/LICENSE
# Add one line per published data directory as it is created, e.g.:
# !/DATA/WelltonMohawk_2026_Package/
# !/DATA/WelltonMohawk_2026_Package/**
!/DATA/USGS_canal_gates_v1/
!/DATA/USGS_canal_gates_v1/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- experiment scripts
# Only the scripts that produce published numbers and figures. The manuscript-authoring
# tools in this directory operate on the Word files and are working code, not results.
!/scripts/
/scripts/*
# Add one line per published script as it is created, e.g.:
# !/scripts/rerun_all_results.py
# !/scripts/record_environment.py
!/scripts/download_usgs.py
!/scripts/identify_gate_law.py
!/scripts/discharge_coefficient.py
!/scripts/validate_gate_law.py
!/scripts/model_error_envelope.py
!/scripts/control_comparison.py
!/scripts/archive_diagnostics.py
!/scripts/make_figures.py
!/scripts/make_tables.py
!/scripts/second_structure.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- published results
# The files the manuscript and the Supplementary Material cite by name, plus the tables
# and figures built from them.
!/results/
/results/*
!/results/*.json
!/results/tables/
!/results/tables/**
!/results/figures/
!/results/figures/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- re-excluded everywhere
# These rules come last so they win over the allowances above.

# Uzbek-labelled working copies of published figures
*_uz.*

# Editor backups and generator scratch
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# Python bytecode and tool caches
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Raw API payloads. The package README and scripts/download_usgs.py both state that
# these are rebuildable on demand, so they are never published -- and this line keeps
# them out even if a future allowlist entry above is written too broadly.
/DATA/.raw_cache/

# Local environments and packaging products
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# IDE, OS, log and temporary files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
~$*
